  ('living-well-with-roommates', 260, 'List the bills your home shares, such as rent, power, internet and water, and note whose name each one is in.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 261, 'Spot a roommate''s new haircut, plant or poster and say one kind word about it.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 262, 'Pick up the mail scattered on the counter and sort it into a small pile for each person.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 263, 'Help a roommate on moving day by holding doors and keeping the hallway clear.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 264, 'Breathe slowly for one minute with your eyes closed when voices and footsteps fill the home.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 265, 'Agree on a reminder date before each bill is due, so nobody has to scramble or feel nagged.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 266, 'Use a shared calendar or whiteboard to flag busy evenings, so nobody is surprised by guests or noise.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 267, 'Clean the lint trap after your load of laundry so the dryer is ready for the next person.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 268, 'Discover which local spot a roommate loves most, and visit it together sometime if they''d like.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 269, 'Write a friendly note on the shared board if you have guests coming, with the time they will leave.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 270, 'Check whether you owe anyone in the house for a recent shared purchase, and settle it today.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 271, 'Try a walk and talk in crisp fall air when a topic feels too heavy to face across a table.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 272, 'Water the shared plants if you notice the soil is dry, and mention it so nobody waters twice.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 273, 'Watch the sunset from a window or the yard with whoever wants to join.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 274, 'Charge your devices away from your bed so your room stays a place for rest.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 275, 'Pause before you send a frustrated message about money, and come back to it after a glass of water and a few slow breaths.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 276, 'Ask "Is there anything I do that bugs you a little?" and receive the answer with a calm thank you.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 277, 'Clear the drain catcher in the shower after you wash your hair.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 278, 'Let a roommate share a story without interrupting, even if it runs a little long.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 279, 'Remind yourself that wanting time alone is ordinary, and does not mean you dislike the people you live with.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 280, 'On a snowy winter morning, check with your housemates about keeping the heat steady overnight so the pipes stay safe.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 281, 'Respond to a roommate''s gentle request today with "Sure, thanks for telling me," and leave it there.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 282, 'Carry the recycling out with a roommate and chat on the short walk to the bins.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 283, 'Greet a housemate''s visiting friend or relative warmly and by name.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 284, 'Give your roommates a heads up before an early start, so the sound of your alarm is not a surprise.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 285, 'Close the curtains together at dusk in winter to keep the warmth in, and chat about how cozy the place feels.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 286, 'Keep a slip of paper handy to jot down a small gripe, then decide tomorrow if it is still worth raising.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 287, 'Keep the hallway clear of your bags and coats so everyone can pass easily.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 288, 'Put on a favorite album while you clean and ask if anyone wants to add a song.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 289, 'Hand back a borrowed book or umbrella with a short thank you, ideally before the owner needs it.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 290, 'Split the spring cleaning of the shared rooms with your roommates, one simple task each.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 291, 'Text instead of calling through the walls when you need something from a housemate in another room.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 292, 'Store your bathroom things in your own basket or shelf to keep the counter clear.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 293, 'Set out a bowl of clementines on a winter morning for anyone who wants one.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 294, 'Let a quiet "not tonight, thanks" be enough when you would rather stay in, without making excuses.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 295, 'Ask in early spring whether anyone wants to swap rooms or rearrange shared furniture before the lease renews.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 296, 'Bring up chilly nights with your roommates on a quiet evening, from extra blankets to warmer slippers.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 297, 'Hang a small hook by the door for keys so nobody has to hunt for theirs.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 298, 'Check in on a roommate who is home sick and see if they need anything from the store.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 299, 'Turn your desk or chair so it faces a window or a plant instead of the door.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 300, 'Read through the move-in notes or photos from when you arrived, so everyone remembers the condition the place was in.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 301, 'Agree with your roommates on a quiet hour for weeknights, then write it on the whiteboard together.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 302, 'Put a fresh liner in the trash can after you empty it, ready for the next person.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 303, 'Join a roommate''s hobby for a few minutes, whether it''s sketching, gardening or a video game.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 304, 'Block out an hour on your own calendar for a hobby, and protect it as kindly as any other plan.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 305, 'Take a few dated photos of each shared room before someone moves out, and save them in your shared house folder.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 306, 'Pause before replying to a group chat message that stung, and answer only once you feel steady.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 307, 'Notice if a roommate has had a long week and take one of their chores off their hands.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 308, 'Swap stories with a housemate about the funniest thing that happened to each of you lately.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 309, 'Find out how each roommate prefers to hear about overnight guests: a message, a chat or a note.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 310, 'Decide together how the security deposit will be divided before anyone moves out, and write it down so it is clear.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 311, 'Offer a sincere compliment to a housemate about something they added to the shared space.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 312, 'Accept a roommate''s help graciously when they cover a chore for you, and say thank you.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 313, 'Build a playlist together for a road trip or a long cleaning session.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 314, 'Dim the lights in your room an hour before bed on a dark winter evening.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 315, 'Share your work or travel plans for the coming days with your roommates, so they know when the home will be quiet or busy.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 316, 'Gently check in with a roommate who seems quieter than usual, and let them know you are around.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 317, 'Wipe down the fridge handle and microwave door, the spots everyone touches.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 318, 'Carry two chairs out to a sunny spot on the first warm day of spring and see who wants to join you.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 319, 'Tuck a pair of earplugs by your bed for nights when the home stays lively late.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 320, 'Check how much notice your roommates would like before a longer visit from family or a friend.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 321, 'Speak for yourself in house talks today, using "I would like" instead of "We all think."'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 322, 'Scrape your plate into the compost or trash right after eating, before the food dries on.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 323, 'Decorate the front door together for autumn with paper leaves or a small wreath.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 324, 'Spend a few minutes in a nearby garden or green space during a busy weekend at home.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 325, 'Invite each roommate to add a note to the emergency list, such as an allergy, and include only what they choose to share.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 326, 'Notice one assumption you hold about a roommate''s habits, and ask them about it with real interest.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 327, 'Mop up the melted snow by the entry after everyone comes in from a winter evening.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 328, 'Study quietly in the same room as a roommate who would like a reading or homework buddy for the evening.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 329, 'Shower at a time that suits the house if the pipes are loud, and ask whether early or late is better.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 330, 'Leave a little breathing room after a disagreement before the next house chat, and open it with a light, kind check-in.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 331, 'Revisit a house rule that no longer fits on a calm spring afternoon, and ask everyone how the change lands.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 332, 'Set a timer for ten minutes and do a quick living room reset with whoever is home.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 333, 'Pick up how to say good morning in a housemate''s first language, and try it out at breakfast.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 334, 'Celebrate the comfort of your own space by adding one cushion, print or color you love.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 335, 'Offer a small gesture of goodwill the morning after a tense evening, like saving your roommate the comfy seat on the couch.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 336, 'Share news early, like a friend coming to stay, so your roommates have time to say how they feel about it.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 337, 'Close the curtains on a hot summer afternoon to keep the shared rooms cool for everyone.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 338, 'Learn a game, recipe or skill from a roommate who is good at it, if they would enjoy teaching you.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 339, 'Share any worry about a guest calmly and in private, rather than in front of the guest.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 340, 'Jot down how you feel after a disagreement with a roommate, then underline one thing you are ready to let go of.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 341, 'Accept a "no" from a roommate without arguing, and thank them for being honest with you.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 342, 'Brush the crumbs off the kitchen table after breakfast so the next person has a clean spot.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 343, 'Pin up a list of fun free things to do nearby for everyone in the house.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 344, 'Agree together where shared items live, so nobody has to search a roommate''s room for them.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 345, 'Say thank you out loud when a roommate pays their share on time, since noticing it keeps money talks friendly.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 346, 'Picture your roommate''s side of a disagreement for one quiet minute before you carry on talking.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 347, 'Share the remote, the couch and the good lamp, taking turns choosing what to watch.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 348, 'Give a housemate the comfy seat on movie night.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 349, 'Wish a roommate a peaceful evening as you head to your room, so the closed door feels friendly.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 350, 'Hold a short, relaxed house meeting on the porch on a warm summer evening to check how the bill split is working.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 351, 'Swap stories with your housemates on a rainy evening about the funniest thing that has happened at home.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 352, 'Return a borrowed dish to the shared cupboard as soon as it is washed and dried.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 353, 'Jot down a new roommate''s favorite foods so you can keep them in mind for the next potluck.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 354, 'Sit under a tree on a mild spring day with a book, enjoying your own company.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 355, 'Plan a simple farewell evening for a roommate who is moving, like a movie night at home or a picnic in the park.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 356, 'Welcome feedback at the next house meeting by asking, "What is one thing we could do better as a home?"'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 357, 'Make room on the bathroom shelf for a new roommate''s things before they move in.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 358, 'Say goodnight to whoever is still awake before you head to bed.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 359, 'Pause before saying yes to plans, and check whether you truly have the energy tonight.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 360, 'Remind a departing roommate to forward their mail, and offer to text them if anything still arrives after they go.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 361, 'Tell each roommate one thing you enjoy about sharing a home with them, in person or in a short text.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 362, 'Pause before you leave the kitchen tonight and ask yourself, is this how I would hope to find it?'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 363, 'Snap a group photo on a happy evening, if everyone is comfortable with it, and share it with the house.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 364, 'Notice how restful your room feels tonight, and choose one small change to try tomorrow.'),
  ('living-well-with-roommates', 365, 'Close the day by thinking of one thing you appreciate about the people you live with, and tell one of them soon.')
) as v(slug, day, task)
